# Build-context trimming for `docker build`. This only affects what gets sent
# to the Docker daemon before a build starts -- Dockerfile.app/.llm/Dockerfile
# each COPY only the specific paths they need, so nothing here changes what
# ends up inside any image.
#
# NOTE: do NOT blanket-exclude *.gguf -- Dockerfile.llm needs
# gemma-4-12B-it-Q8_0.gguf and nomic-embed-text-v1.5.f16.gguf present in the
# build context by exact name. Every other model is excluded below by exact
# filename, because the daemon transfers the whole context before the first
# COPY runs: a model left in costs its full size on every single build, whether
# or not any Dockerfile asks for it.

.git
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
backups/
logs/
data/
VAPT/
samples/
documents/
"aa audit evidence samples/"
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/
qa/
scratch/
.claude/
.vscode/
*.exe
*.pem
gemma-2-2b-it-Q4_K_M.gguf
# Dropped from Dockerfile.llm when the bundle went 12B-only. Leaving it here
# unexcluded shipped 5 GB to the daemon on every build for nothing.
google_gemma-4-E4B-it-Q4_K_M.gguf
*.tar
*.zip
# A git worktree of this same repo, created by a local tool. No Dockerfile
# reads it, and it grows a second copy of the tree into every build context.
.kilo/

# Nothing below is COPYed by any Dockerfile here (app takes src/, config/,
# docker/ and "Sample report.docx"; llm takes the two .gguf models; the db
# image takes init.sql). Excluding them keeps the build context from carrying
# the PyInstaller output and build leftovers to the daemon on every build.
dist/
build/
temp_clean_repo_export/
.pytest_cache/
